Title: GREYHARBOR
Episode: 108 "King Tide"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

EXT. GREYHARBOR DOCKS - DAWN

King tide lifts the planks until the harbor looks ready to step onto land.

Mara carries a copy of the ledger in a fish crate. Lila walks beside her with two sealed envelopes.

LILA
One for Hale. One for the county clerk.

MARA
The clerk loses paper.

LILA
Not if I already mailed it to his wife.

INT. SALT HOUSE COLD ROOM - MORNING

The cold room hums intact, frost bright along the shelves.

Mara opens a locker and removes a dry bundle of ledger pages.

MARA
Tobias kept copies of his copies.

Danny stands guard at the door.

DANNY
Family trait.

INT. EDDA'S KITCHEN - DAY

Edda works dough on the floured counter. Mara reads the copied pages aloud.

Edda kneads hard with her right hand, folding the dough until it shines.

EDDA
Black Osprey isn't a boat. It's Hale's shell company.

MARA
You knew?

EDDA
I suspected. Knowing costs more.

INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - DAY

Hale waits by Tobias's desk. Mara enters with Lila and Gideon.

HALE
You are late.

MARA
The tide argued.

Cole steps from behind the file cabinets, badge on his belt.

COLE
Mara always did let water make her decisions.

Lila drops one envelope. Gideon reaches for a wrench.

EXT. COURTHOUSE STEPS - DUSK

Rain starts as Mara hands the ledger copies to a clerk who looks too young to be useful.

Hale watches from the curb, expression unreadable.

HALE
Copies are not evidence if nobody can authenticate the book.

MARA
Then arrest the book.

Danny stands behind her, pale but upright.

INT. FERRY OFFICE - NIGHT

The Blue Gull's horn groans outside. Danny sits on Gideon's desk, turning a blue fishhook between his fingers.

DANNY
I died in that skiff, Mara. This is the part after.

MARA
Then make the after useful.

Danny nods and pockets the hook.

EXT. GREYHARBOR DOCKS - NIGHT

Mara, Edda, Danny, Gideon, and Lila stand at the end of the pier while the king tide slaps their boots.

The town lights flicker one by one.

Out past the shoals, a boat with no running lights turns away from Greyharbor.

MARA
Let it run.

EDDA
You sure?

MARA
No. But I am done chasing shadows without a witness.

The boat disappears into fog.

FADE OUT.
